<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN NATIONS CUP COLLATED RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN NATIONS CUP COLLATED RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results from the</p>
<p>weekend's African Nations Cup qualifying matches:</p>
<p>Group One:</p>
<p>In Harare:</p>
<p>Zimbabwe 0 Ghana 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 45,000</p>
<p>Standings     P  W  D  L  F  A  PTS</p>
<p>    Ghana     2  1  1  0  2  1  4</p>
<p> Zimbabwe     1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p>   Angola     1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p>Next match:</p>
<p>Zimbabwe v Angola, Harare, February 24</p>
<p>Group Two:</p>
<p>In Bouake:</p>
<p>Ivory Coast 1 Benin 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Guel Tchiressoa (12th minute)</p>
<p>Att: 20,000</p>
<p>In Bamako:</p>
<p>Mali 1 Algeria 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Bassala Toure (63rd min)</p>
<p>Att: 40000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Mali	   2  2  0  0  3  1  6</p>
<p>    Algeria	2  1  0  1  4  2  3</p>
<p>Ivory Coast	2  1  0  1  2  4  3</p>
<p>    Benin	  2  0  0  2  1  3  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Benin v Algeria, Cotonou, February 24</p>
<p>Mali v Algeria, Bamako, February 24</p>
<p>Group Three:</p>
<p>In Dakar:</p>
<p>Senegal 0 Egypt 0</p>
<p>Att: 50,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Senegal    2  1  1  0  2  1  4</p>
<p>    Egypt	2  0  2  0  1  1  2</p>
<p>    Morocco    1  0  1  0  1  1  1</p>
<p>    Ethiopia   1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Ethiopia v Egypt, Addis Ababa, February 23</p>
<p>Senegal v Morocco, Dakar, February 23</p>
<p>Group Four:</p>
<p>In Conakry:</p>
<p>Guinea 1 Tunisia 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Abdoul Salam Sow (49th min)</p>
<p>Att: 50,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Guinea			 2  2  0  0  4  2  6</p>
<p>    Tunisia			2  1  0  1  2  1  3</p>
<p>Central African Republic     1  0  0  1  2  3  0</p>
<p>    Sierra Leone		 1  0  0  1  0  2  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Central African Republic v Tunisia, Bangui, February 24</p>
<p>Guinea v Sierra Leone, Conakry, February 24</p>
<p>Group Five:</p>
<p>In Yaounde:</p>
<p>Cameroon 4 Namibia 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Patrick Mboma (3rd, 85th), Jean-Jacques Misse Misse</p>
<p>(38th, 48th)</p>
<p>In Nairobi:</p>
<p>Kenya 1 Gabon 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Michael Muiruri (70th)</p>
<p>Att: 35,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Cameroon	 2  1  1  0  4  0  4</p>
<p>    Kenya	    2  1  0  1  1  1  3</p>
<p>    Namibia	  2  1  0  1  1  4  3</p>
<p>    Gabon	    2  0  1  1  0  1  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Kenya v Cameroon, Nairobi, February 23</p>
<p>Namibia v Gabon, Windhoek, February 23</p>
<p>Group Six:</p>
<p>In Accra, Ghana:</p>
<p>Liberia 1 Togo 2 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Liberia - Jonathan Sogbie (24th)</p>
<p>Togo - Bachirou Salou (26th), Assignon Komlaga 67th)</p>
<p>In Dar-es-Salaam:</p>
<p>Tanzania 1 Zaire 2 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Tanzania - Said Kitizo (79th)</p>
<p>Zaire - Mbuyo Kitimba (52nd), Ngalabula Kayu (85th)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Togo	 2  2  0  0  4  2  6</p>
<p>    Zaire	2  1  1  0  2  1  4</p>
<p>    Liberia    2  0  1  0  1  2  1</p>
<p>    Tanzania   2  0  0  2  2  4  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Tanzania v Liberia, Dar-es-Salaam, February 23</p>
<p>Togo v Zaire, Lome, February 24</p>
<p>Group Seven:</p>
<p>In Blantyre:</p>
<p>Malawi 0 Zambia 2 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers: Hilary Makasa (40th), Denis Lota (83rd)</p>
<p>Att: 40,000</p>
<p>In Maputo:</p>
<p>Mozambique 3 Mauritius 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Chiquinho Conde (55th), Sergio Faife (62nd),</p>
<p>Jossias (65th)</p>
<p>Att: 30,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Zambia	2  2  0  0  3  0  6</p>
<p>Mozambique	2  1  0  1  3  1  3</p>
<p>    Malawi	2  1  0  1  2  3  3</p>
<p>    Mauritius   2  0  0  2  1  5  0</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Malawi v Mozambique, Blantyre, February 23</p>
<p>Mauritius v Zambia, Bellevue, February 24</p>
<p>The top two teams in each group qualify for the finals in</p>
<p>Burkina Faso in February next year along with the hosts and</p>
<p>holders South Africa.</p>
